# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# bot working files
bot/.cache/

# local admin inbox (runs on your PC, never deployed)
.data/

# Acquired source data. Never committed, and the reason is licensing before it
# is size: UFOCAT is copyright CUFOS and its codebook requires written
# permission to reproduce or publish extracted material, and NUFORC's terms
# forbid redistribution. Pushing either to a public repository *is* publishing
# them. Every file here also exceeds GitHub's 100MB limit, so a commit would
# fail anyway, but that is the lesser reason.
/UFO Data/

# Local tooling only: the Python venv that reads .accdb (this machine has no
# Microsoft ACE driver) and its pip cache. The ingest *scripts* live in
# scripts/ingest/ and are versioned; only the environment is ignored.
/.tools/

# Extracted intermediates. Regenerable from UFO Data/ by rerunning the
# extractor, and derived from licensed sources, so never committed.
/.pipeline/

# Guard, not a description. Docker Desktop's disk image lives at
# D:\Git\Websites\Docker, outside this repo, which is where it belongs: it is
# multi-GB, constantly rewritten while containers run, and the Next dev server
# watches this directory tree. The entry stays so that pointing Docker back here
# by accident cannot put a 5GB vhdx in front of git.
/Docker/
